.TH PULSE-REMOTE 1 "2026" "pulse-remote" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pulse-remote \- Remote audio control for PulseAudio/PipeWire
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pulse-remote-server
.br
.B pulse-remote-desktop
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pulse Remote provides a web interface and desktop application to control audio
volume on Linux systems running PulseAudio or PipeWire.
.PP
.B pulse-remote-server
is the backend daemon that serves the WebSocket API and web UI.
.PP
.B pulse-remote-desktop
launches the Electron desktop wrapper around the web UI.
.SH USAGE
.SS Server
Enable and start the user service:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
systemctl --user enable --now pulse-remote.service
.RE
.fi
.PP
Web interface available at:
.PP
.RS 4
http://localhost:8448
.RE
.SS Desktop App
Launch from your application launcher or run:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
pulse-remote-desktop
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/pulse-remote-server
Backend server binary.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/pulse-remote-desktop
Electron desktop launcher.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/pulse-remote.service
systemd user service unit.
